.TH VALIDATE-AUTONOMOUS-DELIVERY-SET 1 "September 2026" "autonomous-run-governance 0.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
validate-autonomous-delivery-set \- validate an explicit delivery set read-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B validate-autonomous-delivery-set.sh
.BR --repo " PATH"
.RB [ --staged ]
.RB [ --intended " PATH ..."]
.RB [ --allow-historical-whitespace " PATH=RAW_SHA256 ..."]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validates every changed tracked file plus explicitly named untracked delivery
files. With
.BR --staged ,
every intended path must exactly match the index candidate. It reports
unrelated untracked paths, rejects ignored paths, symbolic
links, traversal, duplicates, missing files, directories, and trailing
whitespace, and proves that the Git index and worktree state did not change.
.PP
DE: Das Ergebnis beschreibt die beabsichtigte Liefermenge. Es fuehrt weder
Staging noch Commit, Push, Pull Request oder Merge aus.
.PP
EN: The result describes the intended delivery set. It performs no staging,
commit, push, pull request, or merge.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --repo PATH
Git worktree to validate.
.TP
.B --intended PATH
Repository-relative intended path. In worktree mode it names an untracked
delivery file; in staged mode repeat it for every staged path.
.TP
.B --staged
Validate the exact staged candidate. Historical allowances are restricted to
newly added files and bind their bytes in the Git index.
.TP
.B --allow-historical-whitespace PATH=RAW_SHA256
Permit trailing whitespace only for the explicitly approved, immutable
historical file at the exact repository-relative path and raw SHA-256. The file
must also be named by
.BR --intended .
In worktree mode the file must be untracked; in staged mode it must be newly
added. Repeat the option for multiple files. Hash, path, content, or necessity
drift fails closed.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the explicit delivery set passed. Two means invocation, repository,
path, whitespace, dependency, or immutability validation failed.
.SH NOTES
Invoke the Bash entrypoint through Bash because ZIP extraction may not preserve
executable bits. On Windows use the PowerShell entrypoint. Both call the same
Python 3 validation core and therefore use the same error classes.
.SH SEE ALSO
git(1), validate-autonomous-phase-result(1), validate-autonomous-gate-evidence(1)
